    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "###  Read Me\n\n### OTP Tool – Validate OTP\n\n**Purpose**\n\nValidates a submitted OTP against the OTP stored in Redis and creates an authenticated session when verification succeeds.\n\n**Workflow Inputs**\n\n| Input | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `session_id` | Unique session identifier |\n| `email` | Email associated with the OTP |\n| `otp` | Submitted six-digit OTP |\n| `session_ttl` | Authenticated session lifetime in seconds |\n\n**Validation Process**\n\n1. Validate that the submitted OTP is a six-digit number.\n2. Retrieve the OTP record from Redis using `otp:{session_id}:{email}`.\n3. Check whether the OTP exists and has not expired.\n4. Check whether the maximum of three incorrect attempts has been reached.\n5. Compare the submitted OTP with the stored OTP.\n6. If incorrect, increment the mismatch count while preserving the remaining OTP expiration time.\n7. If the third incorrect attempt is reached, return a maximum retry response.\n8. If correct, create an authenticated session in Redis using `session:{session_id}`.\n9. Delete the OTP record after successful authentication.\n\n**Possible Response Statuses**\n\n| Status | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `OTP_INVALID_INPUT` | Submitted OTP is not a valid six-digit number |\n| `OTP_MISSING_OR_EXPIRED` | OTP does not exist or has expired |\n| `OTP_MAX_RETRY_REACHED` | Maximum of three incorrect attempts reached |\n| `OTP_MISMATCH` | Submitted OTP does not match |\n| `OTP_VALIDATED` | OTP successfully verified |\n\n**Redis Records**\n\n- OTP record: `otp:{session_id}:{email}`\n- Authenticated session: `session:{session_id}`\n\n**Notes**\n\n- OTP mismatch count is initialized at zero.\n- Maximum allowed incorrect attempts: 3.\n- OTP expiration is preserved during mismatch updates.\n- Authenticated session expiration is controlled by `session_ttl`.\n- OTP is deleted after successful validation.",
        "height": 1088,
        "width": 992,
        "color": 4
      },
